<task id="014" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rung 3 — structural detectors (`Detectors/`): calendar-invite, e-sign completion, invoice #, court/e-filing</title>
    <phase>Wave 1 — Server: enrichment + deterministic engine</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>011</dependencies>
    <blocks>015</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a new `Detectors/` subsystem of deterministic structural detectors feeding the live engine; resolves category + invoice/event + obligations that downstream Responsive Intelligence consumes; respects ADR-024 / ADR-045 + bff-extensions governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-rungs</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement Rung 3 — structural detectors — as an `IAssociationRung` backed by a NEW `Detectors/` folder under `Services/Communication/Engine/`. Each detector inspects the `NormalizedMessage` envelope (subject, body, attachments, headers) for a deterministic structural signal and emits a `RungMatch` plus resolved category/entity/obligation metadata in the 0.70–0.95 confidence band:

    • **Calendar-invite detector** — iCal/`text/calendar` attachment or invite headers → resolves an `sprk_event` association + event category.
    • **E-sign completion detector** — DocuSign/Adobe Sign "completed" signals → resolves category + obligation ("executed document").
    • **Invoice-number detector** — invoice-number pattern in subject/body/attachment → resolves invoice association + `invoice` category.
    • **Court / e-filing detector** — court/e-filing notice patterns → resolves category + obligation (deadline/response).

    Detectors resolve category + invoice/event target + obligations (obligations[] feed W5 Responsive Intelligence). Runs for inbound AND outbound (direction symmetry). Do NOT implement the confidence→status ladder (task 015) — emit `RungMatch` + metadata with confidence + provenance; task 015 maps to status.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer, Association Engine rung author. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-024 (regarding family), the engine/rung contract from task 011, ADR-045, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Comfortable authoring a small, extensible detector abstraction (one detector per structural signal, easy to add more).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new `Detectors/` folder holds four structural detectors (calendar-invite, e-sign completion, invoice #, court/e-filing) behind a `IStructuralDetector` abstraction, aggregated by a rung-3 `IAssociationRung`. Detectors emit `RungMatch` in the 0.70–0.95 band plus resolved category + invoice/event target + obligations[] with provenance, symmetric across directions. Build clean; per-detector + symmetry tests pass; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 011 delivered the engine + `IAssociationRung`/`RungMatch`. Task 014 owns rung 3: deterministic structural signals that are stronger than participant correlation (rung 2) because they identify the KIND of communication (an invite, an executed contract, an invoice, a court notice) and often the exact related record. These signals also produce category + obligations metadata that W5 Responsive Intelligence turns into Events/Tasks/Notifications (FR-19) — so rung 3 is the deterministic feeder for the intelligence loop, complementing the AI rung 5 (task 031).

      Component Justification (§11): a new `Detectors/` folder is justified because each detector is a distinct, independently-testable structural signal with a concrete failure mode if absent (e.g., calendar invites never auto-create `sprk_event`); the `IStructuralDetector` abstraction keeps them uniform and extensible (new channel/signal = new detector, per NFR-04) without touching the engine.
    </background>
